I've read through the documents sent regarding this. DmodX would have to be computed by fortity.pca then, depending on how many principal components are kept at this stage (which determines the "model" in the Distance to model measure).

However I am curious regarding how it relates to the squared cosine already computed: the squared cosine is also a measure of the distance between the plane of the PCs and the actual data point. If I'm not misaken, the cosine taken is that of the angle between the point, the intersection of PCs and the projection of the point on the PCs plane, making it very small when the point is far away from the plane.
I can't find information on how those two things (cos2 and DmodX) are used relatively to each other.

