On 2012-Jan-24, at 08:51 , baptiste auguie wrote:
>

> forgot to mention (obvious?) what the idea would transpose to here:
> assign a new class to the output list of plots, and define its print
> method with, e.g. devAskNewPage intertwined.
>

> On 24 January 2012 20:46, baptiste auguie
> <baptist...@googlemail.com> wrote:
>> re displaying a list of plots, when I recently added marrangeGrob in
>> gridExtra, I defined the following print method,
>>
>> function (x, ...)
>> lapply(x, function(.x) {
>>    if (dev.interactive())
>>        dev.new <http://dev.new>()
>>    else grid.newpage()
>>    grid.draw(.x)
>> }, ...)
>>
>> so that an interactive session sees multiple pages (devAskNewPage()
>> could be inserted there instead), but non-interactive devices like
>> pdf, png, etc. produce multiple pages of output (bearing in mind that
>> for some formats you'll need to pass an incremental name like
>> Rplot%2d.png). It's also compatible with ggsave and grid.arrange.

To follow up on this old thread, I've implemented like this:
	https://github.com/jiho/autoplot/blob/master/R/helpers.R

It used devAskNewPlot. It does not ask for the first plot but asks for the following ones, which is different from, say, plot.lm but nicer hopefully (plot.lm asks even for the first plot). It seems to work OK when outputting to a PDF.

The data class (suggestions welcome for a better name) and the print/plot methods could probably move to ggplot2, couldn't they?

